menu "BORING config protocol"

    config WMP_RAM_FAULT_INJECTION
        bool "TEST ONLY: exhaust the DMA-capable internal heap"
        default n
        help
            Never enable for a release. About 20 s after start-up the firmware
            allocates every DMA-capable internal heap block it can and keeps
            them, reproducing a returned unit whose request fingerprints
            failed with that pool exhausted. Use it to check that HELLO,
            GET_STATUS and USB firmware updates still work and how BLE, keys
            and the display behave. Built only with tools/build.sh
            --ram-fault-injection.

endmenu
